 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a value in a JSON document using an RFC 6901 JSON
+Pointer. The empty pointer resolves the full document; object-member and array-element tokens follow
+the standard escaping rules (`~0` for `~` and `~1` for `/`). It throws when the pointer is malformed
+or does not identify a value.
